words are suggested.␀␀␀Custom (manual)␀Picking one applies it straight away.␀␀␀Community preset␀␀␀␀TX dBm␀␀AF␀␀SF is the spreading factor, CR the coding rate, AF the airtime factor. A field applies when you leave it.␀␀␀Max duty cycle␀␀Time on air␀radio2 (MediaMesh)␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. Its SX1262 signals a packet through an I/O expander, not straight to the processor, so it can't hop between two frequencies quickly enough. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀This radio can't run a second frequency. It needs an SX1262, LR1110, LR1121 or LR2021 radio. The Terminal still takes tempradio.␀␀␀␀A second frequency the radio switches to and from, listening and sending there.␀Photos & voice␀␀Everything␀␀Photos & voice: Open TAK photos and voice clips, text stays on the main mesh. Everything: every message goes out on both. Per contact or channel: their Radio setting.␀␀Sent on radio2␀␀Share with them␀MediaMesh only: photo and voice requests and answers stay on radio2, so nodes without it can't swap them with you. Share: requests go out on both, and a photo or clip asked for on the main mesh is answered there.␀␀␀␀Main-mesh nodes␀Client repeat is on, so radio2 is Off: everything, photos and voice too, goes out on the main radio. radio2 goes back to how it was when Client repeat is turned off.␀␀␀250 kHz sends photos and voice about twice as fast; 125 kHz reaches about 40% farther. Both SF7, CR 4/5. Everyone on radio2 must use the same.␀␀Preset␀␀Find MediaMesh␀␀Listening...␀␀␀␀Found␀␀␀Find MediaMesh listens on each preset for about 10 s while nearby repeaters are asked to answer. MediaMesh repeaters answer on radio2 too, so the preset they're heard on is the one in use here.␀␀␀Everyone sharing radio2 must use the same settings. The radio switches between both frequencies, so heavy radio2 traffic costs some main-mesh reception.␀␀␀␀Listen main / radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 preamble␀Switch time␀Packets main / radio2␀␀␀Warnings␀␀␀␀Temporary radio2␀␀␀␀Use other radio2 settings for a while, for example to meet another group. They end on their own or on a restart; the settings above come back.␀␀15 min␀␀2 hours␀Use these for␀␀␀Running now␀Photos, voice messages and push-to-talk on Public and #public. Everyone on the mesh shares these channels, so this is off by default.␀␀␀Photos and voice on Public␀␀Only switch this on in an emergency.␀␀␀␀Battery and sensor readings, for nodes that ask. Your location has its own setting below.␀␀␀Answer telemetry requests␀␀␀Most mesh spam is a single character, because it is the cheapest message to send. Dropped silently: no chat entry, no notification, no sound.␀␀␀Ignore 1-character messages␀Location sharing␀␀␀␀Chosen contacts only␀␀␀␀Anyone who asks␀Sent only when that contact asks, encrypted to them. Nothing is broadcast. Needs "Answer telemetry requests" on. Pick contacts in a contact's menu.␀Share my location when asked␀␀␀␀Off sends them the shifted position your adverts use (GPS > Location privacy).␀␀Exact position to those contacts␀␀␀␀Routing␀1 byte␀␀2 bytes␀3 bytes␀More bytes tell repeaters apart in a big mesh. Repeaters older than MeshCore 1.14 drop 2 and 3 byte packets.␀␀␀␀Multi-byte routing (path hash)␀␀#region␀Region scope (#tag, blank = none)␀␀␀Channel-specific regions can be set in each channel's settings.␀Turn on only if your repeater re-floods just one region. Otherwise it can block logins and direct messages across regions.␀␀Scope direct msgs to region␀Internal (on-board)
External (MMCX)
Auto (legacy, per transmit)␀Only pick External with an antenna fitted to the external socket. After a reboot it starts on the on-board antenna, unless the switch below is on.␀␀LoRa antenna (P4)␀␀␀Starts on the external socket at every boot. Only for an antenna that stays connected.␀␀Always use the external antenna (MMCX)␀␀Reads packets on a background task so a busy screen can't drop them.␀␀␀␀Buffered receive (experimental)␀Resends a message until a repeater echoes it or the recipient ACKs. Turn off to send once only.␀Retry sends until heard␀Signal probe␀␀␀␀Sends a zero-hop advert when no neighbour has been heard for a while, so the signal reading stays fresh. Neighbours only; nothing is repeated.␀␀Minutes, 1 to 1440.␀Auto advert␀Open Advertise app␀␀Send an advert now, or set how often you re-advertise.␀␀Off silences everything below.␀␀A higher-pitched chime, louder on most buzzers.␀Loud alerts␀пЃЁ␀Volume␀␀Vibration␀␀␀Buzz for new messages, even with Sound off. Respects Do Not Disturb.␀␀␀␀Vibrate␀Pulse␀␀␀Gentle␀␀Long␀␀␀␀Plays once for a message, twice for a DM, three times for an @ mention. Tap one to feel it.␀Pattern␀Voice messages␀␀1200 (default)␀␀1600␀␀␀␀3200␀␀␀␀Codec2 bit rate. Higher is clearer but takes longer to send: 1600 uses a third more airtime than 1200, 3200 nearly three times as much. Every VE3 app plays all three.␀␀Recording quality␀␀␀Fills in the treble Codec2 leaves out, so voices sound less muffled. Made on the radio from the voice itself; turn off to hear clips as decoded.␀␀␀␀Brighter voice␀␀AI voice restorer␀␀␀Download voice model␀␀␀␀Play a sound for␀␀␀␀Messages␀␀␀␀Direct messages␀A mention has its own sound and switch, so it can get through when messages are quiet.␀␀@ mentions␀␀Silences the message sounds between these times every day. Messages still arrive.␀␀␀+30m␀␀␀␀-30m␀␀␀␀From␀␀␀␀Until␀␀␀MediaMesh: %s␀␀␀MAIN␀␀␀␀RADIO2␀␀Live␀␀␀␀Heard main / radio2␀Sent main / radio2␀␀Share of packets heard on radio2␀␀␀␀Preamble main / radio2␀␀Profile switches␀␀␀␀radio2 profile␀␀On listens and sends on radio2. Applies with the button below.␀␀Preamble␀␀␀␀Leave the preamble empty and the repeater picks it. Everyone on radio2 must use the same settings.␀␀Apply to repeater␀␀␀о“І␀Bridging␀␀␀␀Both ways␀␀␀Auto␀␀␀␀Separate␀␀␀␀Replies to admins␀␀␀Both␀␀␀␀Main␀␀␀␀Where logins, CLI answers and ACKs go out. Both is the default.␀For Both or radio2 while radio2 is set to Listen.␀␀␀Also on a listen-only radio2␀␀␀␀radio2 can't send right now, so replies only go out on the main radio.␀␀Runs the profile above without saving it, for example to meet another group. The saved radio2 comes back after, or on a reboot.␀1 h␀2 h␀6 h␀Asking the repeater...␀␀Send advert now␀Chat history␀␀␀␀250␀500␀1000␀␀␀␀2000␀␀␀␀No limit␀␀␀␀Older messages in a chat are dropped past this. A very large or unlimited history makes the chat list slower.␀␀␀Keep per chat␀␀␀After this many failed background saves the chat is saved straight away, which can stutter the screen for a moment. Off keeps retrying in the background.␀␀␀Save in the foreground after␀␀␀␀Linked images␀␀␀A link to a picture (.jpg, .png, .gif, .webp, .bmp) in a channel or a DM is downloaded while Wi-Fi is on and shown in its bubble; tap it to see it full size. The picture's server sees this radio's address. Kept on the SD card when there is one.␀␀␀␀Download over Wi-Fi␀Console mode␀␀␀␀Text console␀␀␀␀Experimental. Boots into a text console with no graphical interface: type commands, read replies. Type 'ui' there to come back; if it ever fails to start, the device returns here on its own. Turning it on or off restarts.␀␀␀%s 00m00s
